    description: "**Mechanism.** All 76 TOML dependency-kind nodes share the identical fingerprint hgfp1:87e35a5c97890e5c despite being 67 distinct package names across 76 distinct (name,file) declarations; the structural fingerprint loses all discriminating content because each single-line array-element span does not parse as standalone TOML. toml_config.py creates dependency Symbols with fingerprint=None ('stamped by central post-pass'); the post-pass stamp_symbol_fingerprints (fingerprint.py:246) calls compute_symbol_fingerprint('toml', span, source) -> _tree_sitter_fingerprint('toml', snippet). Each out-of-context array element parses to an ERROR tree (document -> ERROR -> quoted_key + ','); the dependency string body lands between two '\"' leaves but tree-sitter error recovery drops it, so the leaf-token sequence the fingerprint hashes is identical for every dependency.\n\n**Evidence (frozen substrate + live repro).** probe_1_depfp.log: 76 toml deps -> 1 distinct fingerprint / 67 distinct names / 67 stable_ids / 76 ids. The 6 json deps each have a DISTINCT fingerprint that tracks the name (lit -> hgfp1:f79e63e9..., @blocksuite/blocks -> hgfp1:5ef7a060...), so the collapse is toml-specific. toml project-kind nodes (multi-line spans) get 7 distinct fingerprints; only dependency-kind single-line spans collapse. Live: slicing real pyproject.toml dep lines yields genuinely different snippets (ruamel.yaml>=0.18 / rich~=14.3.2 / bcrypt>=4.0) but compute_symbol_fingerprint returns hgfp1:87e35a5c97890e5c for ALL.\n\n**Consequence.** spec §344 defines fingerprint as a content hash ('Detect modifications', 'Changes when implementation changes'). A consumer diffing fingerprints to find which deps changed (version bump, add/remove) sees all 76 as identical and concludes none changed; rich and bcrypt are fingerprint-indistinguishable.\n\n**Related (distinct).** INV-fogum is the TOML-prefix-presence defect (hgfp1: missing) — different. F133.A2 confirms id (76/76) and stable_id (67) individuate the deps correctly; only fingerprint collapses. Cross-links to WI-fanun (fingerprint null populations). Source: dogfood_tranche_07 F133.A1, deterministic frozen read + live compute_symbol_fingerprint."  # f286
